Definitions with the names the protocol table's absolute-path rules use:
NewSessionRequest's cwd (a string) and additionalDirectories (an array of
strings), CreateTerminalRequest's cwd (an optional string), and Diff's path,
which ToolCallContent's diff variant merges through allOf. Validate refuses
a value that is not absolute on the host, by property and index, with a
*ValidationError (0015-MADR-validate-absolute-protocol-paths.md, W1, F1, A4).
The meta declares $/cancel_request and the schema its smallest definition,
which the runtime needs.

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "NewSessionRequest": {"type": "object", "properties": {"cwd": {"type": "string"}, "additionalDirectories": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}}, "required": ["cwd"]},
  "CreateTerminalRequest": {"type": "object", "properties": {"command": {"type": "string"}, "cwd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}}, "required": ["command"]},
  "Diff": {"type": "object", "properties": {"path": {"type": "string"}, "newText": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["path", "newText"]},
  "ToolCallContent": {"oneOf": [
    {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "diff"}}, "required": ["type"], "allOf": [{"$ref": "#/$defs/Diff"}]},
    {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "terminal"}, "terminalId": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type", "terminalId"]}
  ], "discriminator": {"propertyName": "type"}},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
-- want.api --
